asted from a protected file into a file that already existed at the base (modified files are not line-compared), any re-formatting of a protected file's lines (quoting such as `"KEY=v",`, a changed separator such as `KEY: value`, values only, re-encoding: a line matches only when exactly equal once trimmed and at least 8 characters), and a protected file whose lines are all under 8 characters (caught only by an exact whole-file match); the trade-off is over-omission: a new file sharing a common line (such as `NODE_ENV=development`) with any protected file in the workspace, an ignored `.env*` included, is omitted and noted; the pass that lists ignored files has a 180 s timeout (about 6 s per 90k ignored files, so past roughly 2.5 million it fails closed with an error instead of being trusted); the protected-path policy is the operator's workspace policy, not the unit worktree's; an untracked nested git repository is skipped and counted; a diff over the output buffer is refused with a message to scope the inputs; the debugger snapshot is built with the same pinned git environment, the same stripped attribute source (so `text`/`eol` normalization matches the tester's own commit) and the same driver refusal; prerequisite summaries are rendered as JSON-encoded data; a changed auto-collected diff is sent again whole on resume (bounded by the input limit, by design, not as a delta); no repository-configured command runs while the diff is built (fsmonitor, hooks, replace objects, system attributes off; attributes come from a private tree of the worktree's own `.gitattributes` with every `filter` and `diff` assignment removed, so `text`/`eol` normalization still applies and no driver does, where git supports `GIT_ATTR_SOURCE` (git without it ignores the variable silently; see A4a); a filter or diff driver still assigned through `$GIT_DIR/info/attributes` fails closed); a unit whose verifier did not pass keeps that run on the unit (`failedRun`) and a dependent `failure_debugger` may run while the dependency is BLOCKED on it (the one exception to waiting for COMPLETE, recorded in the `operation.ts` lifecycle; a retried dependency is unfinished input again; that debugger runs on a snapshot of the failing candidate, bound to the failed run, and its agent skips the completion oracle entirely (`diagnosticRun`), so neither the configured verifier nor one it discovers after writing a file gates it); a resumed unit is given its current inputs; the `reproduction_command_source` label is derived only together with the command it describes; `authorized_scope` is the operation objective plus the unit's task, which is weaker than a declared file list, and a `replace_task` decision records the scope change (`scopeChange`); a `reproduction_command` is trusted only when operator-configured, otherwise labelled untrusted; caller `inputs` override; anything it cannot derive fails closed naming the input. Tests: `cli/test/specialist_contract_enforcement.test.ts`, `cli/test/specialist_auto_inputs.test.ts` (through `AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run` and `/team`). The verdict-gate clause is WITHDRAWN: `isReviewRole` already covers `reviewer` and `acceptance_reviewer`; `security_reviewer` has no verdict contract and gets the structured-result gate. |
